  "body": "### Describe the bug\n\n# Behaviour\n\nWhen adding a new layout option in a dashboard's settings, it fails to save. For example creating a second layout after the default one for mobile device, it will allow you to input all information, but when the save button is pushed it does not save\n\n# Expected Behaviour\n\nThat the newly created layout will save, and be used.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n# Reproduction\n\nI am not quite sure how to reproduce, as this issue only afflicts one of my boards. To my knowledge I haven't in the creation of that dashboard done anything different.\n\n## Info\n\nWhile I am not sure how to reproduce the bug, I do have some information surrounding it;\n- The bug is contained to one of my Homarr dashboards, the others are unaffected\n- When creating this report I tried creating a new blank dashboard and adding a second layout, it worked as expected.\n- When I try and fail to save a layout on the problem dashboard I get this line in my logs that mentions Layout: `warn: Board not found module=\"createBoardLayout\" code=\"NOT_FOUND\" name=\"TRPCError\"`\n- Settings I am trying to set: 1200 Break for 10 coloms, 0 Break for 3 coloms.\n\n### Impact\n\n# Impact\n\nDue to inability to make additional layouts, use of the particular dashboard on mobile isn't practical.\n\n### Additional information\n\n# Additional Info\n\n- Browser - Opera\n- Homarr was updated to the latest stable release during troubleshooting with docker compose pull, it did not remedy the bug.\n\n### Version\n\n1.46.0\n\n### Installation method\n\nDocker Compose\n\n### Browser\n\nOther (describe in \"additional information\")",
